# The NTS servers every guest keeps its clock by. Compiled into `timesync`, so it
# is part of every measured image, and read by deploy/, which starts the relays
# that reach them.
#
#   <vsock port>  <server>
#
# A guest reaches each server through the host on two ports: the key exchange
# (TLS, server port 4460) on the port written here, and the time packets (UDP,
# server port 123) on the next one up. The relays are blind and the host is not
# trusted with either: the key exchange ends inside the guest, against the roots
# in roots/, and every time packet is authenticated with the keys it agreed.
#
# One server per operator. A clock is taken only when three of them agree, so
# no single operator can move it — and three servers of one operator would let
# that operator do it alone.
#
# Each has to name ITSELF, on port 123, as the server to send time packets to:
# the relay for them is started from this file and cannot follow a key exchange
# that names somewhere else. Netnod names an address of its own and is not here.
#
# A port, once written, keeps its server: releases built from different commits
# share one host, and deploy/ refuses a port two of them read differently.
7100 time.cloudflare.com
7102 ptbtime1.ptb.de
7104 nts.time.nl
7106 virginia.time.system76.com
7108 a.st1.ntp.br
7110 1.ntp.ubuntu.com
